## 2. Wordings and Claims That Would Overclaim (Avoid in Report)

| Category | Overclaiming Wording (Do Not Use) | Methodologically Accurate Wording |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Correctness / Safety** | *"V3–V7 are proven memory-safe / concurrency-correct by passing Loom, 12 pin-projection tests, and 500+ benchmark runs."* | *"V1/V2 defects were caught by expanded Loom models and code review; V3–V7 pass current Loom, unit, and smoke suites, which bounds tested schedules/drop invariants but does not prove absence of concurrency or soundness bugs."* |
| **Wake Precheck Bound** | *"Wake precheck (`W1`) guarantees bounded wake latency and eliminates missed wakes."* | *"Wake precheck (`W1`) is a heuristic optimization that skips the shared rotator RMW when no peer is observed idle; liveness still relies on register/recheck ordering and the 1 ms fallback timer, which is a soft fallback rather than a hard real-time bound."* |
| **SIGPROF Profile Numbers** | *"In V3, `unpark_peer` consumed 14.8% (226/1523) and 15.6% (313/2007) of total CPU time."* | *"`unpark_peer` appeared on 226/1523 (Root) and 313/2007 (Steal) of captured 199 Hz SIGPROF actor-worker stacks (inclusive stack presence, with `libc`/`libgcc`/`pthread`/`vdso` blocklisted; not hardware cycles, total CPU %, or off-CPU wake/futex cost)."* |
| **CPU Accounting** | *"Per-actor-worker CPU efficiency improved by X%."* | *"Process/worker CPU counters include R1 IO, helper/owner threads, and startup padding/drain windows, so CPU totals reflect whole-runtime overhead across those periods rather than pure steady-state actor-worker execution."* |
| **Cross-Source Attribution** | *"Adding Task in V4 and Deque in V5 caused X% speedup over V3."* | *"Sources V3 (`097`), V4 (`09dd`), V5 (`329`), and V6 (`0f81`) are not pooled; isolating component deltas (`Root` vs. `Task` vs. `Deque`, `Z0/Z1`, `W0/W1`) is restricted to same-source comparisons (such as V6 `0f81`)."* |
| **V3 Clock Fairness** | *"`countonly` preserves fairness without time-slicing."* | *"`countonly` removes time-based turn bounds (cooperative poll-count only, no handler preemption) with minimal throughput impact on uniform 100-iter `chain_cross`, but fairness under skewed handler durations or offered-load sweeps was not tested."* |
| **V7 Inline Future Storage** | *"V7 inline storage speeds up actor execution and reduces memory footprint."* | *"V7 inline storage vs. `Box<dyn Future>` is currently in progress (no performance claim yet). Furthermore, it trades early deallocation of the boxed future (while stale `Waker`s retain only `SmallTaskHeader`) for holding the full inline `FullTaskAlloc` until all wakers drop, while ordinary envelope and reply allocations remain unchanged."* |
| **8-Core Scaling (Source 7)** | *"The runtime achieves X% strong scaling from 4 to 8 cores."* | *"The 4-core (`2..5`) to 8-core (`2..9`) comparison spans two distinct L3 cache domains (96 MiB vs. 32 MiB CCDs) while keeping 4 driver (`10..13`) and 4 collector (`14..17`) cores fixed; results reflect heterogeneous multi-CCD throughput scaling on this topology, not homogeneous strong scaling."* |

